      "seed": 1803822986,
      "version": 885,
      "versionNonce": 414318752,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789770651622,
      "created": 1789562840691,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "it is a Binary Search Tree\n\nit has other properties as well:\n 1. A node is either red of black.\n 2. the root is black\n 3. leaves (NIL) are black.\n 4. If a node is red, then its children are black.\n    invariant 5 is the main balancing invariant\n 5. All paths from a node to its NIL descendants \n    contain the same number of black nodes.\n\n \nWhy?   \n \nYou'll see, but first we need to drill this \nproperties in",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "it is a Binary Search Tree\n\nit has other properties as well:\n 1. A node is either red of black.\n 2. the root is black\n 3. leaves (NIL) are black.\n 4. If a node is red, then its children are black.\n    invariant 5 is the main balancing invariant\n 5. All paths from a node to its NIL descendants \n    contain the same number of black nodes.\n\n \nWhy?   \n \nYou'll see, but first we need to drill this \nproperties in",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
