      "seed": 268877059,
      "version": 133,
      "versionNonce": 922829984,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789755083473,
      "created": 1789593902624,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What do these properties actually do?\n\nThe longest path (root to farthest NIL) is no more than twice the length of the\n   shortest path (root to nearest NIL)\n    - Shortest possible path: all black nodes\n    - longest possibl path: alternating red and black\n(show examples AGAIN) be very deliberate. we can start to see why red and black\ncolors are important.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What do these properties actually do?\n\nThe longest path (root to farthest NIL) is no more than twice the length of the\n   shortest path (root to nearest NIL)\n    - Shortest possible path: all black nodes\n    - longest possibl path: alternating red and black\n(show examples AGAIN) be very deliberate. we can start to see why red and black\ncolors are important.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
