      "updated": 1789770565584,
      "created": 1789770466889,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "what is the black height here?\nIt's actually 3. let's count! ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "what is the black height here?\nIt's actually 3. let's count! ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YekHmT-BzHdXptzZmutKs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 557.7213323122962,
      "y": -10057.342146725165,
      "width": 680.9201462175598,
      "height": 735,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0CW",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 740508000,
      "version": 2297,
      "versionNonce": 1282957472,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1789799667143,
      "created": 1789788673026,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The insertion algorithm starts at the root and\nfollows a path downward, using the BST\nproperty to search for where the new key\nbelongs.\n\nIf the new key is smaller than the current node's\nkey, move to the left child.\n\nIf the new key is greater than or equal to the\ncurrent node's key, move to the right child.\n\nEventually, the algorithm will want to move to a\nchild that is NIL. That means it has found the\ninsertion position.\n\nThe new node is then attached at that position\nas either the left or right child of the last real\nnode visited.\n\nIf the tree is empty, the new node simply\nbecomes the root",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The insertion algorithm starts at the root and follows a path downward, using the BST property to search for where the new key belongs.\n\nIf the new key is smaller than the current node's key, move to the left child.\n\nIf the new key is greater than or equal to the current node's key, move to the right child.\n\nEventually, the algorithm will want to move to a child that is NIL. That means it has found the insertion position.\n\nThe new node is then attached at that position as either the left or right child of the last real node visited.\n\nIf the tree is empty, the new node simply becomes the root",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Ih-LcoLe2O3q7BrxD3Zv5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1919.113913478604,
      "y": -11862.320640985241,
      "width": 62.650001525878906,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0CX",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 881452384,
      "version": 321,
      "versionNonce": 917214560,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
